  user_input {
    user_response: "You are an expert Frontend Engineer and Game Developer specializing in hyper-casual mobile web games. \n\nYour objective is to generate a complete, fully functional, single-file MVP (Minimum Viable Product) for a mobile-first web game called \"Chain Reaction\". The entire game must be contained within a single index.html file, including all HTML structure, Tailwind CSS styling (via CDN), and Vanilla JavaScript canvas physics. Do not use external asset files (images/audio)\342\200\224render all visuals procedurally using Canvas API.\n\n### GAME CONCEPT & MECHANICS\n1. Screen State: A 2D physics bounding box filled with 40-50 floating, volatile geometric shapes (Floating Particles).\n2. Particle Behavior: Particles drift slowly in random directions, bouncing off the screen edges. They do not collide with each other initially.\n3. The Trigger: The player gets exactly ONE tap per round. Tapping anywhere on the screen drops a static \"Trigger Spark\" at that exact coordinate.\n4. The Chain Reaction: \n   - When the Trigger Spark expands, any Floating Particle that touches its radius detonates.\n   - Detonated particles stop moving, turn into expanding explosion circles, freeze for 2 seconds, and then shrink and fade out.\n   - Any other drifting particles that touch these secondary explosions also detonate, creating a cascading domino effect.\n5. Win/Loss Condition: The round ends when all explosions have faded. The goal is to clear a target percentage of particles (e.g., clear 70% to win the level).\n\n### JUICE & DOPAMINE REQUIREMENTS (CRITICAL)\n- Visuals: Particles should have vibrant, glowing neon colors. When they explode, create a brief burst of 8-10 tiny debris particles shooting outwards.\n- Audio (Procedural): Use the Web Audio API to generate a sound effect on every single detonation. The pitch of the sound must increase slightly with every consecutive combo hit in the chain reaction (creating a musical escalation scale).\n- UI/UX: Show a live counter of [Particles Cleared / Target] and a massive, satisfying combo counter (e.g., \"12x COMBO!\") that floats up and fades near the latest explosion.\n\n### MVP FEATURE REQUIREMENTS\n- Mobile-First Design: Tailored for a portrait mobile screen aspect ratio but centered gracefully on desktop.\n- Game Loop Screens:\n  1. Start Screen: Title, simple \"Tap to Play\" button, and high score display.\n  2. Gameplay Screen: The active physics canvas with live HUD tracking score, level, and remaining active explosions.\n  3. Game Over Screen: Shows final score, peak combo count, a \"Success / Level Cleared\" or \"Failed\" message, and a prominent \"Share Ghost Link\" button (mocking the viral copy-paste text functionality).\n- Level Progression: Each level increases the total number of floating particles slightly and raises the target percentage required to clear it.\n\n### TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS\n- Use standard HTML5 `<canvas>` for rendering the game field.\n- Use `requestAnimationFrame` for a smooth 60fps physics loop.\n- Use native touch events (`touchstart`) and mouse events (`mousedown`) to register the player\'s single trigger drop accurately.\n- Ensure clean code isolation: State management, Physics/Update Loop, Render Loop, and Event Handlers.\n\nOutput only the complete, self-contained HTML file code block with no markdown explanations outside of the block. Make sure it is completely plug-and-play."
    items {
      text: "You are an expert Frontend Engineer and Game Developer specializing in hyper-casual mobile web games. \n\nYour objective is to generate a complete, fully functional, single-file MVP (Minimum Viable Product) for a mobile-first web game called \"Chain Reaction\". The entire game must be contained within a single index.html file, including all HTML structure, Tailwind CSS styling (via CDN), and Vanilla JavaScript canvas physics. Do not use external asset files (images/audio)\342\200\224render all visuals procedurally using Canvas API.\n\n### GAME CONCEPT & MECHANICS\n1. Screen State: A 2D physics bounding box filled with 40-50 floating, volatile geometric shapes (Floating Particles).\n2. Particle Behavior: Particles drift slowly in random directions, bouncing off the screen edges. They do not collide with each other initially.\n3. The Trigger: The player gets exactly ONE tap per round. Tapping anywhere on the screen drops a static \"Trigger Spark\" at that exact coordinate.\n4. The Chain Reaction: \n   - When the Trigger Spark expands, any Floating Particle that touches its radius detonates.\n   - Detonated particles stop moving, turn into expanding explosion circles, freeze for 2 seconds, and then shrink and fade out.\n   - Any other drifting particles that touch these secondary explosions also detonate, creating a cascading domino effect.\n5. Win/Loss Condition: The round ends when all explosions have faded. The goal is to clear a target percentage of particles (e.g., clear 70% to win the level).\n\n### JUICE & DOPAMINE REQUIREMENTS (CRITICAL)\n- Visuals: Particles should have vibrant, glowing neon colors. When they explode, create a brief burst of 8-10 tiny debris particles shooting outwards.\n- Audio (Procedural): Use the Web Audio API to generate a sound effect on every single detonation. The pitch of the sound must increase slightly with every consecutive combo hit in the chain reaction (creating a musical escalation scale).\n- UI/UX: Show a live counter of [Particles Cleared / Target] and a massive, satisfying combo counter (e.g., \"12x COMBO!\") that floats up and fades near the latest explosion.\n\n### MVP FEATURE REQUIREMENTS\n- Mobile-First Design: Tailored for a portrait mobile screen aspect ratio but centered gracefully on desktop.\n- Game Loop Screens:\n  1. Start Screen: Title, simple \"Tap to Play\" button, and high score display.\n  2. Gameplay Screen: The active physics canvas with live HUD tracking score, level, and remaining active explosions.\n  3. Game Over Screen: Shows final score, peak combo count, a \"Success / Level Cleared\" or \"Failed\" message, and a prominent \"Share Ghost Link\" button (mocking the viral copy-paste text functionality).\n- Level Progression: Each level increases the total number of floating particles slightly and raises the target percentage required to clear it.\n\n### TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS\n- Use standard HTML5 `<canvas>` for rendering the game field.\n- Use `requestAnimationFrame` for a smooth 60fps physics loop.\n- Use native touch events (`touchstart`) and mouse events (`mousedown`) to register the player\'s single trigger drop accurately.\n- Ensure clean code isolation: State management, Physics/Update Loop, Render Loop, and Event Handlers.\n\nOutput only the complete, self-contained HTML file code block with no markdown explanations outside of the block. Make sure it is completely plug-and-play."
    }
  }
