  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing the UI**\n\nI\'m working on integrating the game\'s UI now. I\'m focusing on bringing `App.tsx` into being, so I can start to use it. I\'m considering state management for the game elements, and thinking about integrating the game engine and audio modules. The next step is a fully interactive game.\n\n\n**Refining the State Management**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on state management, particularly for screen navigation, and core game stats. I\'m leveraging `useState` hooks to manage the game screen, level, total score, and peak combo. I\'m working out how to update these states from the game engine. I\'m using `useRef` for the canvas and game engine instance, and I\'ve also implemented handlers for score updates and round end events. The structure is coming together!\n\n\n**Implementing Game Engine Lifecycle**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the lifecycle management of the game engine itself, and thinking about initialization, starting levels, and handling destruction/cleanup. I\'m focusing on the `useEffect` hook to initialize the engine when the game screen becomes active. I\'m taking care to correctly handle score updates and the end-of-round event. I\'m also addressing the crucial cleanup when the game screen is unmounted, to prevent memory leaks and unexpected behavior. This has all been integrated.\n\n\n**Integrating Input & UI**\n\nI\'m now integrating user input directly into the game\'s UI flow. I\'ve implemented event handlers that translate mouse clicks into game actions, passing coordinates to the game engine. I am linking the \"share score\" button to a copy-to-clipboard function that creates a shareable string that links the user to a mock ghost game. I\'m focusing on providing seamless gameplay with intuitive interactions.\n\n\n**Designing the Gameplay Loop**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the gameplay loop and its visual presentation. I\'m focusing on the introduction and startup sequence, and using CSS transitions, shadows, and animations to enhance the experience. I\'m especially focused on the transition between the splash screen and gameplay elements and making the main game UI functional. I\'m trying to make the experience smooth and interactive.\n\n\n**Visualizing Level Progression**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the visual presentation of level progression within the UI. I\'m focusing on the display elements related to level, cleared blocks, total required, and combo indicators. I\'m focusing on how these will be styled and animated, especially the combo counter, to provide clear feedback to the player. I am looking to make the level display intuitive and visually engaging.\n\n\n**Refining Feedback Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now refining the feedback mechanics, particularly for user taps. I\'ve added a visual indicator that appears when the player taps the screen during gameplay, informing them that a reaction is being tracked. I\'m focusing on providing this clear, immediate feedback, and making the cue subtle but noticeable. I\'m also ensuring this feature only appears once the game has started.\n\n\n**Evaluating Round Over**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the visual representation of the round-over screen. I\'m focusing on the messages that communicate victory or defeat. I\'m especially attentive to the visual feedback \342\200\223 the use of color and the subtle drop shadow to provide immediate visual cues. I am also determining how to accurately render the stats, such as the total required and cleared, within the context of the user\'s experience. I am making sure the messaging provides a cohesive and informative experience.\n\n\n**Analyzing Score Visualization**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the live score visualization, including current level progress and peak combo. I\'m focusing on providing dynamic updates to level cleared, total required, and peak combo values. I\'m trying to make the combo display particularly impactful. I\'m working to make the real-time display of the live score intuitive and visually clear.\n\n\n**Designing the \'Round Over\' Button**\n\nI am now focusing on the \"Round Over\" button\'s visual and interactive design. I\'ve considered incorporating icons like `Play` and `RotateCcw` to provide clear feedback. I want it to clearly indicate if the player can proceed or needs to retry. I\'m leveraging Tailwind classes for visual styling, considering hover and active states.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
