ges while applying the new styles, specifically focusing on the positioning, styling, and visual flair of the combo indicator. I\'m focusing on the `absolute top-12 left-0 right-0 px-6 flex justify-between items-end z-40` style. I\'m using Tailwind classes for colors, fonts, and backdrop blur effects to create the visual enhancements needed for the theme.\n\n\n**Implementing Combo Indicator**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dynamic styling for the combo indicator. I\'m focusing on the animation and visual enhancements. The goal is a stylish, eye-catching combo display, using Tailwind classes. I\'m adding a pulse effect and drop shadow using Tailwind classes to highlight the increasing combo. I\'m prioritizing the display of the `Combo` text, then the `x` character.\n\n\n**Refining Existing UI**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI element enhancements, making styling and container adjustments to match the vibrant design while preserving components. I\'ve re-evaluated and am adapting the HUD code for styling, retaining essential elements. I\'m prioritizing class tweaks to ensure the new theme aligns with the original intent. The current design requires a refactoring of the class styles.\n\n\n**Adapting Display Styles**\n\nI\'m now adapting the styles for the \"ROUND_OVER\" screen, focusing on text and background. I\'m swapping out the original classes for updated Tailwind classes and colors, changing `bg-slate-900/95` to `bg-[#0c0c0e]/95`. The goal is a smoother transition with the design theme\'s visual aesthetic.\n\n\n**Styling Button Components**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on button styling, specifically the start game button. I am considering the neon text and card styles to inform the button design. I have a `bg-white/10 text-white border border-white/20` plan, but am thinking of adding glow and animation for the button.\n\n\n**Modifying Canvas Background**\n\nI\'m now adapting the background of the physics canvas to align with the \"Vibrant Palette\" theme. I\'ve decided to modify `engine.ts` to use `ctx.clearRect` rather than a solid fill. This will let the CSS background from parent classes show through, which looks great!\n\n\n**Revising Canvas Background**\n\nI\'ve decided on the final canvas background strategy. After some experimentation, I\'m sticking with `ctx.clearRect` for transparency. I will be changing the colors in the canvas file, from the original hex codes to the theme\'s colors. This approach should preserve visual effects from CSS. I\'ve re-evaluated the engine file.\n\n\n"
