mbo indicator\'s visual effects. I\'m prioritizing the animation and drop shadow to make it more visually prominent during gameplay. I\'m also ensuring the text rendering is optimized for clarity and readability, especially the \'X\' to indicate the combo multiplier. The visual style has to seamlessly blend with the application, of course.\n\n\n**Refining Live Stats Display**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the live stats display. I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy to make sure the level, cleared blocks, and combo indicator are easy to understand. I have improved the combo multiplier display by replacing the old code block with the new code snippet, especially updating the text rendering and styling of the combo multiplier, and ensuring the text rendering is optimized for clarity and readability.\n\n\n**Adding Game Feedback**\n\nI\'m now integrating game feedback elements, starting with a \'Watching reaction...\' message that displays initially. I\'ve also added a prompt instructing the player to tap to drop a spark when the game is live, and I\'ve ensured a proper display on the \'ROUND_OVER\' screen, with appropriate styling to indicate game status. I\'m focusing on UI elements that are clear and responsive, especially after a game over.\n\n\n**Implementing Round Over**\n\nI\'m now integrating the round-over screen. I\'m focusing on the visual feedback when the level is cleared or if the player fails. I\'m implementing dynamic text for \"LEVEL CLEARED!\" or \"FAILED!\" based on the game outcome. I am also updating the description text to make it clear what happened, and including visual indicators for cleared vs. total blocks. I\'m prioritizing making this UI element a quick and clear signal for the player.\n\n\n**Enhancing UI Feedback**\n\nI\'m now integrating the peak combo display into the Round Over screen, focusing on how it communicates. I\'m prioritizing clear visual hierarchy, using mono font for the text and appropriate sizing to make the information prominent. I\'m also implementing a conditional button that changes based on game outcome, updating with \"NEXT LEVEL\" or \"TRY AGAIN\".\n\n\n**Adding Share Score Button**\n\nI\'m now integrating the share score functionality into the Round Over screen, focusing on the visual presentation and responsiveness of the \"SHARE GHOST LINK\" button. I\'m focusing on ensuring its functionality, along with its visual design, by adding effects and appropriate UI. I\'ve also added a \"State Tracking Toast\" element to track the status of the game, including \"tapped\" and \"started\" actions.\n\n\n**Adding Game Hints**\n\nI\'m now integrating hints during gameplay, such as instructions to tap for sparks. I\'ve ensured this message displays correctly when appropriate. I\'ve also focused on the \'ROUND_OVER\' screen, with appropriate styling to indicate game status, and making sure the information is clear to the user.\n\n\n**Improving Round Over UI**\n\nI\'m now revising the \'Round Over\' screen, specifically the visual feedback based on game outcome. I\'m making it dynamic with conditional text and adjusting the description text and visual indicators for cleared vs. total blocks. I am also implementing peak combo display and a conditional button to improve the UI of the round-over screen.\n\n\n**Refining Button State**\n\nI\'m now implementing conditional button states on the round-over screen. The button now updates dynamically to \"NEXT LEVEL\" or \"TRY AGAIN,\" with an accompanying icon. I\'ve focused on ensuring the visual cues clearly indicate the next action. I\'m prioritizing the smooth transition between states.\n\n\n**Adding Notch Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the notch component into the application\'s top section to match the mock up. I\'m focusing on its visual integration with the container screen, making sure it visually fits. I\'m also now updating the canvas layer to have a `bg-gradient-to-b` for visual consistency.\n\n\n"
