make sure to replace the `playDetonate` import too!\n\n\n**Visualizing Field Distortions**\n\nI\'m now focused on visualizing the magnet\'s effect. I\'m aiming for high-quality visual feedback. Think thin grid lines warped by the magnet\'s coordinate for a subtle effect, and nested neon circles rotating in opposite directions at the magnet\'s location when active. Particles will also get trailing arcs. I\'m working through the math for this grid warp, with grid lines every 40px and modifications relative to the active magnet. Splitter projectiles will have bright neon streaks with fade-away tails.\n\n\n**Adjusting Grid Distortion**\n\nI\'m now refining the grid warp effect. I\'ve tweaked the pull power calculations for the magnet and gravity explosions, setting different influence distances to 150 and 120, respectively. I\'m focusing on the visual impact, and the nested pull power values. I\'ve also adjusted grid distortion logic, using `drawX` and `drawY` for calculations.\n\n\n**Refining Grid Effect**\n\nI\'m now refining the grid warp effect within the canvas context. Horizontal lines\' distortion are being considered, especially now that calculations for both vertical and horizontal lines have been completed. I am trying to focus on a consistent and subtle visual effect. Specifically, I\'m working with influence distances for accurate distortion.\n\n\n**Optimizing Warp Rendering**\n\nI\'m now completely satisfied with the subtle rubber-sheet space warp visual! I\'m now documenting the `SplitterSpark` behavior and structure, including the `id`, `x`, `y`, `vx`, `vy`, `life`, and `color` properties. Upon splitter detonation, I\'ll be spawning four of these sparks.\n\n\n"
