o the shop. I\'ve defined `THEME_SHOP_ITEMS` with details: IDs (representing themes), names, descriptions, costs, and color previews for display. I\'m focusing on defining `ParticleTheme`, and thinking about how to seamlessly integrate these into the player experience. I\'ve designed three initial themes: STANDARD, NEBULA, and MATRIX. I\'ll need to define how to apply purchased themes.\n\n\n**Adding Theme Data**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed color data for themes within `THEME_SHOP_ITEMS`. Specifically, the new \"SOLAR\" theme includes \'solar flame oranges\', \'starfire red\', and \'pure gold\' colors, representing an excellent theme the user will enjoy! I also implemented starting the user with 200 shards, loading from, and saving to, `localStorage` for shards. I\'m focusing on ensuring seamless integration of this new data with the rest of the app.\n\n\n**Integrating Game Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating game data more deeply. I\'ve focused on persisting essential game states. Specifically, I\'m now saving and loading upgrades, purchased themes, and the active theme to/from `localStorage`. I\'m updating `startLevel` to pass `upgrades` and `activeTheme`. I\'m also examining `handleRoundEnd` to understand how shards are earned and how that could be improved.\n\n\n**Displaying Shard Earned**\n\nI\'ve updated the `handleRoundEnd` function to calculate and store the shards earned after a level. I\'m focusing on ensuring this data is visually displayed, specifically the breakdown of shards earned from base, perfect clear, and combo bonuses. This will provide valuable feedback to the player.\n\n\n**Visualizing Sparks**\n\nI\'m now integrating visual indicators for sparks. Specifically, I plan to display them within the `ROUND_OVER` card, showcasing a detailed breakdown of shard earnings. In addition, I\'ll add little lights in the HUD, beside the \"DROP SPARK\" button, to indicate the number of sparks available, and this will be responsive when they are clicked.\n\n\n**Visualizing Sparks Left**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual representation of available sparks. I\'ve updated the HUD, specifically adding indicators beside the \"DROP SPARK\" button. I\'m ensuring these lights are responsive and update in real-time, displaying how many sparks are remaining using the provided code. I\'m continuing to integrate visual feedback.\n\n\n\n**Refining User Experience**\n\nI\'m now refining the user experience around spark interactions. I\'ve updated the `handlePointerDown` function to enable multiple clicks if sparks are available. Specifically, it now checks `liveStats.sparksLeft > 0` before allowing a click. I\'m focusing on ensuring players can utilize multiple sparks seamlessly.\n\n\n"
