  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Initial Imports**\n\nI\'m currently focused on identifying the necessary imports for this project, particularly within the React environment. I\'ve begun to outline the core libraries and modules needed, including those related to game engine functionality, state management, and audio components. Next I will organize these imports into relevant functional blocks.\n\n\n**Validating Icon Choices**\n\nI\'ve validated the usability of all chosen Lucide icons, confirming their availability. I\'ve remapped the `BadgePlus` icon to the universally compatible `PlusCircle` to guarantee functionality. I\'ve also established mappings between function variables, such as `extraSparks` to `Zap`, and finalized foundational icon selections, for a concise and robust set of icons! Finally, I am preparing the necessary state.\n\n\n**Defining Core State Elements**\n\nI\'m now establishing the primary state variables within the `App` component, including screen management, help visibility, persistent game statistics like level and scores, and currency tracking. I\'m also addressing upgrade modifiers, and intend to integrate local storage for score and currency persistence. I\'m taking care to initialize state from local storage where available.\n\n\n**Implementing Local Storage**\n\nI\'m now integrating local storage to save player progress. I\'m focusing on preserving upgrade states, which I\'ve encapsulated in `chain_reaction_upgrades_v3`, as well as saving purchased themes, keyed under `chain_reaction_purchased_themes_v3`, and also the active theme using `chain_reaction_active_theme_v3`. I\'ve implemented error handling to provide default values in case of storage access issues.\n\n\n**Establishing Game State Variables**\n\nI\'m now focusing on establishing game state variables. I\'m adding tracking for shard stats, live game stats, and win status, and perfect clears, and I\'ve also added ref elements for canvas and game engine. I\'m including pointer event handling references, and score update handlers. I\'m taking care to account for potential local storage errors.\n\n\n**Refining Persistence Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now refining the local storage implementation, specifically focusing on saving game state changes. I\'m adding `useEffect` hooks to ensure data persistence for shards, upgrades, purchased themes, and active themes. I\'ve also integrated try-catch blocks to gracefully handle potential errors during local storage operations, ensuring robust data management even in adverse conditions.\n\n\n**Calculating Shard Rewards**\n\nI\'m now calculating quantum shard earnings based on game outcomes. I\'m taking into account the level, whether there was a perfect clear, and the player\'s max combo. I\'m also updating total shards and total score based on the win conditions. Additionally, I\'m increasing total score, and checking to see if a new high score has been established!\n\n\n**Implementing High Score Logic**\n\nI\'ve added the high score logic, using `localStorage` to save the new high score and update the state when a player achieves it. I am using `useEffect` to start and destroy game levels, but I am now re-evaluating the current state flow.\n\n\n**Handling Pointer Input**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `handlePointerDown` function to manage player interactions. I\'m focusing on accurately calculating the click coordinates relative to the canvas. I\'m also implementing the `deployManualSpark` function to enable manual spark deployment, taking into account canvas dimensions and player sparks remaining. I\'ve re-reviewed the guard statements for proper state management.\n\n\n**Designing Shop Component**\n\nI\'m now drafting the SHOP screen markup within the handheld window. I\'m focused on the layout, ensuring a clear title and a \"back\" button for easy navigation. I\'m implementing the basic structure with a shards tracker header and a back button using Tailwind classes. I\'m aiming for a clean and intuitive design for a better user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Shop UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the SHOP screen. I\'m focusing on incorporating the shards counter and the \"Quantum Research\" title with its subtitle, both styled for visual appeal. I\'m using Tailwind classes for precise layout and typography. I\'ve now added the header components to the shop layout!\n\n\n**Updating Shop Items**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the SHOP screen\'s item listings, focusing on dynamic display of upgrade levels and cost calculations. I am pulling from the `SHOP_ITEMS` data structure, and using the `upgrades` state to display the current level, and a dynamic cost for the next upgrade level, when present. I\'m dynamically choosing the correct icon, for an intuitive user interface.\n\n\n**Implementing Shop Content**\n\nI\'m now focusing on rendering the shop item details. I\'m adding upgrade level indicator dots for each item, to show progression, using a dynamic array based on upgrade level. I\'ve also implemented the logic for displaying the appropriate icons, names, and descriptions for each item, pulled directly from the `SHOP_ITEMS` data. I\'m taking care to ensure that the item data is correctly displayed on the SHOP screen.\n\n\n**Refining Upgrade Displays**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the visual representation of upgrade levels within the shop. I\'m dynamically generating level indicators using a responsive dot system, accurately reflecting the current level and maximum level of each upgrade. I\'m using dynamic arrays to render the dots, with visual distinction between active and inactive levels. I\'m also addressing the visual separation and spacing of the UI elements.\n\n\n**Evaluating Shop Purchase Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the buy action within the shop. I am first checking if the upgrade is maxed. I\'ve now added logic to check if there are enough shards to cover the upgrade cost, using the ternary operator to render either a \"STABLE MAX\" label, or a purchase button with a dynamic cost. I\'m also now updating the state for shard totals, and upgrade levels. I\'ve wired in a sound effect on successful purchase!\n\n\n**Finalizing Button States**\n\nI\'m now completing the shop upgrade button. I\'ve integrated a conditional display for upgrade costs and states. I\'m dynamically rendering either an \"UPGRADE\" button or a \"STABLE MAX\" label, based on shard availability and upgrade levels. The button styling, including hover and active states, is also now fully implemented with Tailwind classes.\n\n\n**Refining Theme Selection**\n\nI\'m now implementing theme selections within the shop module. I\'m dynamically adjusting the display of theme shop items, showing a checkmark for the currently active theme, as well as indicating purchased and unpurchased states. I\'m focusing on providing clear visual feedback on theme availability and active selection. I\'ve wired in the purchase flow for themes, and integrated checks for already purchased items!\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Switching**\n\nI\'m now integrating the logic to switch themes within the application, focusing on dynamic updates to the UI based on the selected theme. I\'m focusing on updating the application state to reflect the active theme, and also managing the local storage for theme persistence. I am now updating color palettes in real-time, based on the selected theme, for an immersive experience!\n\n\n**Refining Theme Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the theme\'s colors. I am setting CSS variables dynamically using the selected theme, for seamless color application across the UI. I have added color override logic, and implemented a helper function to set the root CSS variables, based on the theme selection. This ensures full-application theme consistency.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Purchase Logic**\n\nI\'ve completed integrating the purchase logic for themes, including updating shard counts and saving new purchases to local storage. I\'m also ensuring the active theme updates correctly in the state. I\'ve successfully wired up the audio feedback, so now I\'m working to consolidate the visual feedback for the user.\n\n\n**Refining UI Feedback**\n\nI\'m now consolidating UI feedback for theme purchases, ensuring the visual cues are intuitive and responsive. I\'m focusing on the integration of visual confirmation after a purchase, and I\'m updating the theme selector to reflect the new state. This includes both bought and active states, for a great user experience.\n\n\n"
