  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Slot Machine Addiction**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the core psychological triggers that drive slot machine addiction. Initial research points toward intermittent reinforcement, variable reward schedules, and the illusion of control as major factors. Now I am considering how these elements might be subtly incorporated into \"Chain Reaction\" to enhance engagement, without crossing ethical boundaries.\n\n\n**Analyzing Game Design Aspects**\n\nI am now focusing on applying addictive design principles to the \"Chain Reaction\" game concept. Specifically, I\'m examining how to incorporate a Variable Ratio Schedule of Reinforcement by making rewards unpredictable. Additionally, \"Near Misses\" will have dramatic visual treatments, like special displays with \"NEAR MISS!\" to enhance the feeling of closeness to success and potentially trigger a \"Lucky Chance\" offer. We also have to consider Loss Disguised as Wins (LDWs).\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 905686262
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
