  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Audio Effects**\n\nOkay, I\'m thinking about adding audio effects to `/src/lib/audio.ts`. I plan to implement `playSlotSpin()` which will play a repetitive click sound, perhaps with rapidly increasing frequency. Then, I will add `playSlotStop()` to trigger a bright metallic sound to signify the wheels stopping.\n\n\n**Expanding Audio Design**\n\nI\'m now focused on fleshing out audio cues, adding `playSlotPayout()` for coin chimes and `playNearMissAlert()` for an alarm. I plan to add those to `/src/lib/audio.ts`. I\'ve shifted to a visual design, and I\'m keen on developing a slot machine mini-game, including a \"REACTOR MULTIPLIER REEL\" integrated into the `ROUND_OVER` screen of `App.tsx`. I envision three vertical columns, each with a list of items like emojis to be used in the reels.\n\n\n**Designing Game Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the core slot machine mechanics. I\'ve been thinking about the \"Reaction Combo Payout Roll\" banner and how to integrate a multiplier. I\'m considering a system where the spin result dictates a multiplier applied to the Quantum Shards base payout. The multipliers will range from 1.1x for no matches to 5.0x for a jackpot, with a \"near-miss\" 1.2x multiplier for two matches. I\'m pondering allowing players to buy extra spins or gamble for higher rewards, potentially allowing them to double-down on wins.\n\n\n"
