    thinking: "**Defining New State Variables**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the necessary state variables for the new slot machine functionality. I\'ve pinpointed a persistent `clearStreak` counter stored in local storage, and the state of the slots themselves, including a `slotSpinning` boolean and a `slotReels` array (initialized with [\'\360\237\215\222\', \'\342\232\241\', ...]). My goal is to capture the complete cycle.\n\n\n**Expanding State Variables**\n\nI\'ve added several new state variables to enhance the slot machine. We now have `slotMultiplier`, `slotPayoutMessage`, and `slotGlowIndex` for visual feedback. Also, a `slotHasSpun` boolean ensures a spin happens each level. There\'s also `isNearMiss` and `nearMissSparksPurchased` to capture near failures and continue costs. Lastly, I\'ve defined `coinExplosions` for visual reward feedback. I also revisited how rewards are calculated on a win. Clear streak is incremented, and base shards are defined.\n\n\n**Refining Reward Implementation**\n\nI\'ve set `slotMultiplier` to `1.0` and `slotPayoutMessage` to `\"\360\237\222\245 PULL LEVER TO INCUBATE MULTIPLIER! \360\237\222\245\"`. I\'m now calculating the `shardTotalGained` but holding off on adding it to `shards`. Instead, I\'ll store the pre-multiplied value in `preMultipliedTotal` for later multiplication during the spin. This delay and the chance element, makes everything more engaging. The perfect win message will read: \"REACTION COMPLETED! BASE PAYOUT = 200 shards. SPIN FOR REACTION MUTATOR (Multiplier from 1.1x to 5.0x!)\". Reels will show e.g. `[\'\360\237\216\260\', \'\360\237\216\260\', \'\360\237\216\260\']` and they can earn up to 1,000 shards.\n\n\n"
