  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Game Reset Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `startGame` function in detail, specifically its conditional logic for resetting game parameters after a round ends. I\'m focusing on how the game handles level progression, score reset, and combo metrics based on the previous round\'s outcome \342\200\223 win or loss. I\'m interested in optimizing this logic.\n\n\n**Refining Continue Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"second chance\" logic. The goal is to avoid resetting the level if the player purchases a continue after a near miss. I\'m focusing on integrating a visual cue, a \"SECOND-CHANCE SPARK TRIGGER,\" on the `ROUND_OVER` screen. I\'ve designed the condition of the near miss in `handleRoundEnd(win, stats)`, so I can create a custom dialog when the level ends and they got very close to winning.\n\n\n**Evaluating Reward Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the reward structures post-round, especially the shard payouts. I\'ve fleshed out the logic for determining shard awards based on wins, losses, and streaks. For wins, I\'ve defined a formula incorporating level progression, clear streaks, perfect clears, and max combos. I\'ve also implemented a consolation payout for losses, which awards a small shard amount for \"participation.\" Currently, I\'m working out how to best display and communicate these reward structures to the player.\n\n\n"
