  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the custom screen**\n\nI\'m now focused on the custom `ROUND_OVER` screen\'s design. The key is integrating the High Alert/Near-Miss section when `isNearMissScreen` is true. I\'m planning a \"Second Chance\" button and \"Forfeit Counter\" within that special section.\n\n\n**Refining the Winning Screen**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the winning screen when `didWinLast` is true. I\'m excited about the **MULTIPLE REEL SPIN ZONE**: a slot machine integration. I\'m focusing on the glowing \"PULL REACTOR MUTATOR LEVER!\" button (only if `!slotHasSpun`), forcing player engagement. The \"PROCEED\" button is only active post-spin, reinforcing this mechanic!\n\n\n**Constructing the Re-Engagement Flow**\n\nI\'m now designing the JSX structure for the \"ROUND_OVER\" screen. The flow includes an immediate \"RE-ENGAGE SEQUENCE\" button. My focus is crafting the UI elements; I\'m making sure it\'s visually appealing. I\'m carefully writing out the new JSX for the screen, paying close attention to any typos or missing elements. The code will replace lines 918-1033 of `/src/App.tsx` via `edit_file`.\n\n\n**Developing the near-miss alert**\n\nI\'m working on the UI for the \"CRITICAL NEAR-MISS!\" alert section. I\'ve been focusing on the design elements, like the red-themed styling using Tailwind classes. It needs to convey the high-stakes situation. The warning icon, background, and text all combine for a strong warning. I\'m hoping to use animation to bring emphasis to the warning, specifically with an \"INSTABILITY WARNING\" text and alert triangle.\n\n\n**Analyzing Target Progress**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the live statistics and target progress updates. I\'m focusing on the visual display of the grid completion percentage. The goal is to accurately show progress and trigger the warning message, while also working on the design to make it highly visible. I\'ll need to link this progress to the overall user flow, and add UI elements to communicate the urgency.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Spark Purchase**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the \"buySecondChanceSpark\" button. I\'m focusing on the shard cost calculation, making sure `shards < 50 * (nearMissSparksPurchased + 1)` is correct. The styling includes a disabled state and a shadow for visual cues, which need more analysis. I\'m considering how to handle the button\'s visual state upon clicking to make sure the user has a visual cue.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Buy Button**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the \"SECURE SECOND-CHANCE SPARK\" button. I\'m focusing on its visual representation and conditional states. I\'m considering using Tailwind classes to implement different visual cues for available/unavailable states. I will ensure that the user gets the proper visual cues. I\'m working on the design to communicate the price and shard count.\n\n\n**Designing the Forfeit Button**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"FORFEIT SWEEP\" button for the \"ROUND_OVER\" screen. I\'ve designed the button\'s appearance with a focus on visual distinction. I\'ve used Tailwind to style the button; it needs to clearly communicate the forfeit action. I want to convey both the consequence and the consolation aspects. The JSX structure is in place, and I will be working on the interactivity next. I\'ll test the `onClick` handler and visual cues for user feedback.\n\n\n**Refining UI Considerations**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual cues for different game states. I\'m focusing on the component that displays the game\'s active state. I\'m carefully analyzing its visual logic and styling, making sure it visually updates to reflect win or near-miss conditions. I\'m also looking into the different icons to be used for the display of these conditions, and making sure that the icons clearly communicate the appropriate game states.\n\n\n**Evaluating Bonus Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual display for \"PERFECT CLEAR\" and \"STREAK\" bonuses. I\'m crafting the JSX structure using Tailwind to create distinct, eye-catching elements. The \"PERFECT CLEAR\" bonus uses a pulsating star icon. The \"STREAK\" bonus has an animated flame icon and shadow effects, to communicate a high-dopamine state. I want the icons and animations to be clear and engaging for the user.\n\n\n**Iterating on Visuals**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual display logic for game state information. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the display for \"PERFECT ALL-CLEAR\", \"LEVEL CLEARED!\", and \"TACTICAL FAULT!\" situations. I\'m focusing on Tailwind classes for dynamic text colors and shadow effects. The goal is to visually reinforce these distinct game outcomes.\n\n\n**Assessing State Text**\n\nI\'m now refining the text display based on game outcomes. I\'m making sure the text updates correctly for \"PERFECT CLEAR\", \"DID WIN LAST\", and \"REACTION DIED\" conditions. I\'m using dynamic string templates within the JSX to show the appropriate information. The goal is to clearly and concisely show the user their current progress.\n\n\n**Analyzing Combo Progress**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying the live combo stats. The goal is accurate visual representation using JSX, integrating combo metrics with the overall design. I\'m prioritizing the visual impact of the `PEAK COMBO` element.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Reel Design**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visuals for the reactor combo mutator display. I\'m focusing on the pulsing effect to highlight this critical combo. I\'m incorporating the four pulsing dots around the `REACTOR COMBO MUTATOR` text to draw the user\'s focus. I\'m leveraging the `Trophy` icon and the animated bounce to add visual engagement.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Slot Symbols**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visuals for the spinning slot reels. I\'m focusing on the animation of the slot reels during the spin. I\'m leveraging the `animate-pulse` class for visual engagement. I\'m ensuring there\'s a strong visual cue to represent the reels, which needs to highlight the reel symbols.\n\n\n**Visualizing Multiplier Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the slot multiplier details, focusing on the visual display. I\'m dynamically updating the `slotPayoutMessage` based on the `slotMultiplier` value, using text that is readable and appealing. I\'m applying conditional styling with Tailwind, particularly using a pulsating effect and the `bg-gradient-to-r` effect, to highlight high multipliers in the UI. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s clear when a high multiplier has been achieved.\n\n\n**Calculating Reward Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying the shard reward breakdown. I\'ve integrated the base reward and grid multiplier details into the UI. I\'ve used Tailwind classes for visual consistency and clarity. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s clear for the user to understand.\n\n\n**Refining Lever Visuals**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the slot lever\'s visual state. I\'m focusing on the `pullSlotLever` button when `slotSpinning` is true. I\'ve designed the button\'s appearance to change when disabled. I\'m focusing on the `cursor-not-allowed` state and the button\'s background. I\'m also ensuring the text color reflects the disabled state. I\'m going to also implement a loading animation to provide user feedback.\n\n\n**Designing the Bonus Awards**\n\nI\'m now integrating visuals for the consolation shard extract. I\'m focusing on the non-winning state. The design includes a gradient background, border, and shadow. I\'m crafting the text to convey a sense of a disguised win. The `animate-bounce` effect brings attention to this section, and I\'m updating the component based on whether `didWinLast` is true.\n\n\n**Visualizing Button States**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visuals for the \"START\" and \"RESTART\" buttons, focusing on their conditional states. I\'m leveraging Tailwind classes to ensure they appear disabled when the reel is spinning. The design includes a clear visual distinction. I\'m making sure that the buttons become visually available when the slot has spun.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Play Button**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"PROCEED\" and \"PULL MUTATOR LEVER\" button\'s visual states, depending on `didWinLast` and `slotHasSpun`. The text and styling dynamically adapt using Tailwind classes. I\'m focusing on ensuring clear visual feedback, especially with the Play icon and disabled states.\n\n\n**Implementing the Re-engagement**\n\nI\'m now integrating the re-engagement features into the `ROUND_OVER` screen. I\'m focusing on the \"RE-ENGAGE SEQUENCE\" button, which leads back into the game and the \"ENTER UPGRADE SHOP\" for the player to utilize the shop function. I\'m going to also implement the shareScore function for improved user interaction.\n\n\n"
