  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Extinction Shockwave**\n\nI\'ve initiated the process of defining `triggerExtinctionShockwave`. My focus is on writing the logic, specifically how it interacts with and extinguishes nearby explosions. I\'m considering using a red critical smoke ring effect to visualize the wave.\n\n\n**Implementing Extinction Logic**\n\nI\'ve added the `triggerExtinctionShockwave` method, integrating it to extinguish nearby explosions. The logic is now in place and working within a 150px radius. I have added code to extinguish explosions triggered by collision handlers when the DECAY particle is triggered. I\'m exploring an effect, such as, \"CHAIN BROKEN!\" when triggering.\n\n\n**Refining Extinction Logic**\n\nI\'ve refined the `triggerExtinctionShockwave` method to extinguish nearby explosions when triggered. I\'ve integrated this into the collision handlers. This creates a hazard for players who now must actively herd cells away from the anti-matter trap centers. The extinction logic is operational and creates a massive hazard.\n\n\n"
